NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_Quiet

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_Quiet -- [.S.], BOOL

    FUNCTION
        Same function as List.mui/MUIA_List_Quiet.

        Think about using it when you insert/remove several entries
        one by one, it will go much faster.
        In all cases all changes which can be done later are delayed.
        Quiet_Full mean that no notify caused by changes in the list will
        be made, while Quiet_Visual will done them (but delayed to after
        the Quiet_None).

    SPECIAL INPUTS
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_None       same as FALSE.
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_Full       all values but FALSE and MUIV_NList_Quiet_Visual (-2).
        MUIV_NList_Quiet_Visual

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_Insert, MUIM_NList_Remove
NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SelectChange

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SelectChange -- Receive a selection-change notification.

    INPUTS
        Notification trigger; BOOL. The local getter returns TRUE, not a
        stored selection state.

    FUNCTION
        NList emits TRUE when pending line-selection changes are delivered.
        Notifications can be coalesced by the class notification machinery;
        one notification does not identify one particular row. Use Select or
        NextSelected to inspect state.

        Setting the attribute yourself does not select entries. Character
        selection does not use all the same line-selection helper paths. For
        subclass callbacks with row and state arguments, use
        MUIM_NList_SelectChange; its default handler returns zero.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_SelectChange, MUIM_NList_Select, MUIM_NList_NextSelected

NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_ShowDropMarks

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_ShowDropMarks -- [ISG], BOOL

    FUNCTION
        Same function as List.mui/MUIA_List_ShowDropMarks.

    DEFAULT
        FALSE

    SEE ALSO
        MUIA_NList_DropMark
NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SkipChars

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SkipChars -- [ISG], char *

    FUNCTION
        Same function as Floattext.mui/MUIA_Floattext_SkipChars.
NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SortType

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SortType -- Store the primary comparison value.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get/notify; LONG. Default MUIV_NList_SortType_None
        (0xF0000000).

    FUNCTION
        Store the value supplied to MUIM_NList_Compare and the corresponding
        CompareHook2 message field. The default Stricmp comparison ignores
        it; its meaning belongs to the custom comparison policy.
        SortType_None is a stored value, not a local switch that disables
        Sort.

        Setting this attribute does not sort the list and does not clear the
        internal sorted flag. If the comparison policy changes, explicitly
        sort the whole list before relying on incremental sorted insertion.
        The setter leaves the tag for superclass notification; get returns
        the stored value.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_Sort, MUIM_NList_Sort2, MUIM_NList_Sort3,
        MUIA_NList_CompareHook2

NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SortType2

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SortType2 -- Store the secondary comparison value.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get/notify; LONG. Default MUIV_NList_SortType_None
        (0xF0000000).

    FUNCTION
        Store the value supplied to MUIM_NList_Compare and the corresponding
        CompareHook2 message field. The default Stricmp comparison ignores
        it; its meaning belongs to the custom comparison policy.
        SortType_None is a stored value, not a local switch that disables
        Sort.

        Setting this attribute does not sort the list and does not clear the
        internal sorted flag. If the comparison policy changes, explicitly
        sort the whole list before relying on incremental sorted insertion.
        The setter leaves the tag for superclass notification; get returns
        the stored value.

    SEE ALSO
        MUIM_NList_Sort, MUIM_NList_Sort2, MUIM_NList_Sort3,
        MUIA_NList_CompareHook2

NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SourceArray

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SourceArray -- [I..], APTR

    FUNCTION
        Same function as List.mui/MUIA_List_SourceArray.
NList.mcc/MUIA_NList_SourceInsert

    NAME
        MUIA_NList_SourceInsert -- [I..], struct MUIP_NList_InsertWrap *

    FUNCTION
        Same as DoMethod(obj,MUIM_NList_InsertWrap,...)
        with ... same as the contents of the passed struct,
        but at init.

